      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the accusatory finger gesture",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the hand with the finger pointing upward, which is a common gesture of accusation or 'I am right' in meme culture. This gesture visually reinforces the confrontational tone of the text, implying that the user (or the meme's author) is asserting their correctness in dismissing systemic racism by focusing on individual slave ownership statistics. The projection is implicit, not explicit with deictic pronouns, but the gesture functions as a deictic pointer to the user's stance.",
